{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-75238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3},\\,{P}_{2}={1,2,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/46b590842cb6dd1cb994318be3a35ef0f7782542d3a74c4f788180577ab50301.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/193d8dc290095a750fe6c7fb6a5d6e75efb342e213f8aabc8fb7921cd335242e.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/a8c9191c43ca304fee01dbb4298c5312f1993ebd25aef266dd9a4828af5f25d5.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=4 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =1+4+4+7 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6f3cfb8c181868ac54be4428865734405aa859d836bb65de800904e7281da39d"} {"question" "q-75238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "21"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3},\\,{P}_{2}={2,3,4},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/01edff0feb1bf7545526c3eb258ffb608a982fae094d83a0512b006ec930a60f.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/335148bb25604ed918640c6a21feb7de3ede3a2cd340fbc5288442bbe3ed3d6d.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/b0c98c2e3785d1b0ccdd8675f89f6a83372dfc1f1ca60c76c638871d56add91b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,2)=6 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,3)=5 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,3)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =4+6+5+7 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6f3cfb8c181868ac54be4428865734405aa859d836bb65de800904e7281da39d"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "34"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=6 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=6+3+3+0=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6f3cfb8c181868ac54be4428865734405aa859d836bb65de800904e7281da39d"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-75254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=7 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=4 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=7+4+4+1=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6f3cfb8c181868ac54be4428865734405aa859d836bb65de800904e7281da39d"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3,4},\\,{P}_{2}={0,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/c30acb7cb94886e612675d5e64838961134e8d09e5d88c1d803067832f4b173e.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/e5c92768512480b16fcca735126b303c4ca372d22a5c735fc8cea1588a3c5811.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/b015f94b135ca669c0711057c7245982eb8f0257e4947a603571f2826364b8fa.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,0)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=4 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,0)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6f3cfb8c181868ac54be4428865734405aa859d836bb65de800904e7281da39d"} {"question" "q-122982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e0823f37f80c28ae634aacf05780e8"} {"question" "q-122982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "30"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2bd853916bbe739fe73d4448a6034ce89e